# psp104 tests

For now, we use the same test cases for the psp as for the Berkeley BSIM model
(see gnucap-models/bsim/tests/b4_*.gc).

## Test variations

$ make check TEST_PARAMSET_SELECT=compiled # default
tests compiled paramsets, psp_{n,p}mos.so

$ make check TEST_PARAMSET_SELECT=interpreted
tests interpreted paramset based on generic model

## Ratings

Each test result is rated according to is level of agreement with simulation
results obtained with ngspice + osdi

+ Basic sanity check passed - result appears physically reasonable
++ Good qualitative match with ngspice results
+++ Quantative match up to numerical tolerance with ngspice results

